rgest indie devs in  the uk  spanning across multiple locations  worldwide they were founded in 2005  and focused on flash games until  breaking into the console space in 2010  with who's that flying  monsters probably stole my princess and  one thousand tiny claws  they started working with devolver  digital in 2013 with a game called foul  play  which devolver published for both steam  and xbox live arcade  mediatonic partnered up with devolver  once again in 2014 for the release of  hadafall boyfriend which came out on  windows  mac linux ps4 and the ps vita  long left the vita but never in all  their years have they had such an early  smashing success like they've seen with  fall guys  number four it's perfect for updates  because of the fact that fall guys is a  battle royale comprised of a series of  mini games  the game is tailor-made to be updated  and perfect for the seasonal model  that's proven to be so successful with  other games in the space  mediatonic has already added one new  minigame and are sure to have countless  others in the works behind the scenes  in my opinion this one will ultimately  be what determines their long-term  success  how long can they keep the top streamers  interested in playing the only way to do  that is by keeping the game fresh with  smart updates that are spaced out  just the right amount there's a very  careful line here between  updating too much and not updating  enough mediatonic will certainly have to  prove they can find that line if they  want to maintain  their success before we get into the one  reason for concern let's go ahead and  talk about the fifth reason that i  believe fall guys is poised for  long-term success  and that is more platforms no not more  hexagon platforms  more video game platforms fall guys has  taken the world by storm despite the  fact it isn't even available on xbox  switch ios or android  the devs have already made it known  they're focused on steam and ps4  for now but they also stated